nixos-config
============

GNOME provides the desktop and Software center. NixOS manages hardware, core
tools and services; Flatpak supplies standalone graphical apps. System and
application updates are separate and manual.

Prepare your machine
--------------------

Review hosts/desktop/settings.nix and preserve your actual hardware module,
boot configuration, account and installed system.stateVersion baseline.
Never copy another machine's filesystem identifiers.

Use bash scripts/prepare.sh --help for the required preparation arguments.
Prepare a writable checkout, then follow setup (see docs/SETUP) to check, build
and apply it. Preparation locks dependencies without activating the system.

After applying, verify a new login and administrative access before rebooting.
Keep the current terminal open until those checks pass.

Guides
------

Read setup (see docs/SETUP) before applying this configuration.

A README or host-side check does not establish native build, activation or
boot success on your machine.
